# plugin-adj-rib-in-features - verify adj-rib-in plugin --features output
# Tests that ze plugin bgp-adj-rib-in --features answers that the plugin
# declares no features: it exits 0 and prints nothing. The plugin decodes no
# NLRI or capability and returns no YANG module of its own, so its feature
# list is empty. A unit test cannot decide this: it is the shipped binary's
# dispatch of the plugin's registration through `ze plugin`.
# reject=stdout:pattern= reads both streams of the command, so stderr must be
# empty too.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze plugin bgp-adj-rib-in --features
expect=exit:code=0
reject=stdout:pattern=\S
